Derivation and modification notice (AGPL-3.0 sections 4 and 5)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This program is a modified version of Satvisor
(https://github.com/satvisorcom/satvisor), which is itself derived from
TLEscope (https://github.com/aweeri/TLEscope). Both are licensed under
AGPL-3.0, and copyright in the unmodified portions remains with their
respective authors.

Carried over substantially unchanged: the SGP4 tracking engine, 3D globe and
scene rendering, sky view, orrery, pass predictor, Doppler analysis, SatNOGS
browser, antenna rotator and rig control, theme system, and the
draggable-window canvas.

Changes made in this version:

  - Added an Anatomy window: 15 spacecraft modelled as parts lists over a
    shared 66-component library, with 3D geometry generated procedurally from
    the parts list and mass/power budgets derived from the same data.

  - Added a Link Budget window: phased-array and RF link modelling driven by
    the live tracking state, deriving elevation, slant range and off-nadir
    steering angle from the tracked satellite and configured observer.

  - Removed the optional external-device feedback target and its two
    authenticated GitHub Packages dependencies, replacing it with a stub, so
    the project builds from a clean checkout without registry credentials.

  - Replaced the data mirror with an independently operated one
    (https://github.com/maxmoneycash/orbital-works-data) fetching from the
    same upstream sources, CelesTrak and SatNOGS.

  - Rebranded to Orbital Works: application name, icons, metadata, desktop
    bundle identifiers, and persisted storage key prefixes.

  - Replaced GitHub Pages deployment with Vercel, and resolved Open Graph
    tags against the deployment domain at build time.

  - Added a Satellite Designer window: a language model selects hardware from
    the component library and the existing procedural geometry pipeline renders
    the result, graded by the same mass and power analysis as the rest of the
    fleet. Served by a Vercel function using the AI Gateway.

  - Added a Phased Array window and a Waveform window, both computed from the
    existing patternDb / OFDM / STARLINK_MCS tables rather than new physics.

  - Added a Constellation window comparing the licensed Starlink shell
    architecture against objects matched in the live catalogue.

